ty Policy and any rights you have under\napplicable consumer‑protection law that cannot be waived, the site and products are provided <strong>\"as\nis\" and \"as available\"</strong>, without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including\nmerchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non‑infringement.</p>\n<h3>1.13 Limitation of liability</h3>\n<p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, Nottera will not be liable for any indirect, incidental,\nspecial, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits, data, or goodwill. <strong>Our total\nliability for any claim will not exceed the amount you paid for the product(s) giving rise to the\nclaim.</strong> Nothing limits liability that cannot be limited by law.</p>\n<h3>1.14 Billing disputes and fair‑use</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Billing questions:</strong> if you believe there is a billing problem, <strong>contact us first</strong> at\n  hello@mynottera.com — most issues are resolved within 24 hours. Filing a payment dispute in bad\n  faith (for example, after receiving the product, or in place of a return) is a breach of these\n  Terms. We may contest such disputes with evidence (including tracking and delivery confirmation),\n  recover amounts owed, and decline future service.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Return and promotion fair‑use:</strong> we may refuse or limit orders, returns, refunds, or discounts\n  where there is repeated, excessive, or bad‑faith activity, false claims, resale, or promotion\n  abuse.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Verification:</strong> we may require identity or payment verification and may cancel orders that\n  cannot be verified.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>1.15 Indemnification</h3>\n<p>You agree to indemnify and hold Nottera harmless from claims, damages, and expenses (including\nreasonable legal fees) arising from your breach of these Terms, misuse of the site, or violation of\nlaw or third‑party rights.</p>\n<h3>1.16 Dispute resolution; arbitration; class‑action waiver</h3>\n<p><strong>Please read carefully — this affects your legal rights.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Informal resolution first.</strong> Before any formal proceeding, you agree to contact us at\n  hello@mynottera.com and attempt to resolve the dispute informally for at least 30 days.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Binding arbitration.</strong> Any dispute not resolved informally will be resolved by <strong>binding\n  individual arbitration</strong> administered by the American Arbitration Association under its Consumer\n  Arbitration Rules, rather than in court, except that either party may bring an individual claim in\n  <strong>small‑claims court</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Class‑action waiver.</strong> Disputes are arbitrated <strong>only on an individual basis</strong>; you and Nottera\n  waive any right to participate in a class or representative action.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Opt‑out.</strong> You may opt out of arbitration within <strong>30 days</strong> of first accepting these Terms by\n  emailing hello@mynottera.com with your name, order/email, and a statement that you opt out.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Time limit.</strong> Any claim must be filed within <strong>one (1) year</strong> after it arises, to the extent\n  permitted by law.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Where these provisions are not permitted, they do not apply to you.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>1.17 Governing law</h3>\n<p>These Terms are governed by the laws of the <strong>State in which Nottera is established</strong>, without regard to conflict\nof law rules, and subject to §1.16.</p>\n<h3>1.18 Changes</h3>\n<p>We may update these Terms at any time. Changes take effect when posted with a new \"Last updated\"\ndate. Continued use or purchase constitutes acceptance.</p>\n<h3>1.19 Force majeure</h3>\n<p>We are not liable for delays or failures caused by events beyond our reasonable control, including\nnatural disasters, war, strikes, carrier disruptions, customs actions, pandemics, or governmental\nmeasures.</p>\n<h3>1.20 Miscellaneous</h3>\n<p>If any provision is unenforceable, the rest remains in effect. Our failure to enforce a provision is\nnot a waiver. You may not assign these Terms; we may. These Terms and the policies referenced here\nare the entire agreement between you and Nottera.</p>\n<h3>1.21 Contact</h3>\n<p>Nottera — support@mynottera.com.</p>"
