    "body": "<p><strong>Last updated: July 2026</strong></p>\n<h3>5.1 Limited warranty</h3>\n<p>Nottera warrants that its physical products are free from <strong>manufacturing defects in materials and\nworkmanship under normal use</strong> for <strong>three (3) years from the date of delivery</strong> (the \"Warranty\nPeriod\"). This warranty covers <strong>genuine factory/manufacturing defects only — not damage caused by\nmisuse, accidents, improper care, or normal wear.</strong> It is provided to the <strong>original purchaser</strong> and\nis <strong>non‑transferable</strong>.</p>\n<h3>5.2 What is covered</h3>\n<p>Genuine manufacturing faults under normal, intended use — for example, seams that fail, foam that\nprematurely and permanently loses its supportive structure beyond normal wear, or a cover or zipper\nthat fails under normal use.</p>\n<h3>5.3 What is not covered</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Normal wear and tear; gradual, expected softening or minor loss of loft over time.</li>\n<li>Damage from misuse, accidents, improper cleaning, or failure to follow care instructions.</li>\n<li>Stains, odors, or discoloration caused by use.</li>\n<li>Cosmetic variations (color or texture) inherent to the materials.</li>\n<li>Items without proof of purchase, or purchased from an unauthorized reseller.</li>\n<li>Comfort preference (a warranty covers defects, not personal comfort — pillows have their own 60‑Night Trial, and pillowcases have a change‑of‑mind window on unopened items; see the Return &amp; Refund Policy).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>5.4 Remedy</h3>\n<p>If a valid claim is approved, we will, <strong>at our discretion, repair, replace, or refund</strong> the affected\nproduct. Replacement may be with the same or a comparable product if the original is unavailable.\nThis is your <strong>sole and exclusive remedy</strong> under this Limited Warranty.</p>\n<h3>5.5 How to claim</h3>\n<p>Email support@mynottera.com with your <strong>order number, proof of purchase, and photos or video</strong> of the\ndefect. We may request additional information or, in some cases, return of the item.</p>\n<h3>5.6 Limits</h3>\n<p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, this Limited Warranty is in lieu of all other warranties, and\nour liability is limited as set out in the Terms of Service (§1.12–1.13). This warranty gives you\nspecific legal rights; you may also have other rights under your local law, which are not affected.</p>"
